course: dictionary
lesson: 6080
title: A word for mixed family roots
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a group of people. Mestizo is one of them. Read the clues around it: «Meetings of peoples created new peoples, cultures and languages, like mestizo culture in Mexico.» The words next to it mention Mexico and culture, so the word tells us about a group of people and where they come from.
explain: Mestizo is a Spanish word. It describes a person whose family came from two places: Spanish (European) ancestors and Native American ancestors. Ancestors are the people in your family from long ago. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "like Spanish and Native American culture in Mexico" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: The word also works as a describing word. «Mestizo culture» means the customs and ways of life that grew from both sides. The word can be a noun too: a person is a mestizo. Many Latin Americans call themselves mestizo, so it is a word people use about who they are.
fact: Mestizo is a Spanish word.
fact: «Mestizo» means a person with both Spanish (European) and Native American ancestors.
fact: The word is used especially in Latin America, such as Mexico.
fact: As a describing word, «mestizo culture» means culture that mixes both sides.
fact: Many Latin Americans call themselves mestizo today.
exercise: «Meetings of peoples created new peoples, cultures and languages, like mestizo culture in Mexico.» What does mestizo describe here? | A river in Mexico | * Culture that mixes Spanish and Native American roots | A language from France | A kind of food
exercise: Which place is the word mestizo especially used in? | * Latin America | Japan | Antarctica | Canada
exercise: «Creole languages, such as Haitian Creole, grew from French and African languages.» Find and copy the word that names a language made by mixing other languages. | African | languages | * creole | French
test: A mestizo person has ancestors from which two groups? | * Spanish (European) and Native American | French and Antarctic | Spanish and Japanese | Only Native American
test: Which sentence uses mestizo as a describing word? | Mestizo is a river | The mestizo ran fast | They ate mestizo for dinner | * They admired the mestizo culture of Mexico
exam: Ella says mestizo means a mixed fruit salad. Is she right? | No, it is a Spanish dance | * No, it describes people with Spanish and Native American ancestors | Yes, it means a mixed up town | Yes, it means a mixed fruit salad
